{"plan":{"schema":"whiteboard-plan/1","planId":"wj_246f720363704899ab33121b4f92df65","revision":1,"goal":"The learner will understand how gradient descent repeatedly steps against the slope to reach a minimum, by following three steps on f(x) = x squared.","audience":"a curious learner","durationSeconds":60,"language":"en","voice":"whiteboard-default-v1","quality":"whiteboard-1080p-v1","sourceRefs":[],"scenes":[{"id":"s1","startFrame":0,"endFrame":360,"learningPoint":"Gradient descent finds the lowest point of a curve by repeatedly stepping downhill.","visualIntent":"Axes with the curve f(x) = x squared sampled from x = -3.5 to 3.5 at 15 points. A dot at x = 3, height 9. A circle marks the bottom at x = 0, labelled 'minimum'.","narrationSummary":"Gradient descent finds the lowest point of a curve. Picture standing on this hill at x equals three, and walking downhill step by step.","facts":[{"text":"starting point x","value":3,"provenance":"claim"},{"text":"f(3) = 3 squared","value":9,"provenance":"computed"},{"text":"minimum at x","value":0,"provenance":"computed"}],"illustration":false},{"id":"s2","startFrame":360,"endFrame":840,"learningPoint":"Each step moves x against the slope, scaled by a learning rate.","visualIntent":"Write the rule as text: new x = x − rate × slope. Below: slope of x squared = 2x. A short tangent line at x = 3 labelled 'slope 6', and 'rate = 0.25' written beside it.","narrationSummary":"The slope tells which way is uphill. For x squared the slope is two x, so six at x equals three. We step the other way, scaled by a learning rate, here a quarter.","facts":[{"text":"slope of x squared","provenance":"claim"},{"text":"slope at x = 3 is 2 × 3","value":6,"provenance":"computed"},{"text":"learning rate","value":0.25,"provenance":"claim"}],"illustration":false},{"id":"s3","startFrame":840,"endFrame":1380,"learningPoint":"Repeating the rule moves x closer to the minimum each time.","visualIntent":"Three arrows on the curve hopping from x = 3 to 1.5 to 0.75 to 0.375. Side table written as text: 3 − 0.25×6 = 1.5; 1.5 − 0.25×3 = 0.75; 0.75 − 0.25×1.5 = 0.375. Heights labelled 9, 2.25, 0.5625, 0.140625.","narrationSummary":"Step one: three minus a quarter of six gives one and a half. Step two: zero point seven five. Step three: zero point three seven five. Each step halves x, and the height drops toward zero.","facts":[{"text":"x after step 1: 3 − 0.25 × 6","value":1.5,"provenance":"computed"},{"text":"x after step 2: 1.5 − 0.25 × 3","value":0.75,"provenance":"computed"},{"text":"x after step 3: 0.75 − 0.25 × 1.5","value":0.375,"provenance":"computed"},{"text":"height after step 1","value":2.25,"provenance":"computed"},{"text":"height after step 2","value":0.5625,"provenance":"computed"},{"text":"height after step 3","value":0.140625,"provenance":"computed"}],"illustration":false},{"id":"s4","startFrame":1380,"endFrame":1800,"learningPoint":"The learning rate controls step size: too small is slow, too big overshoots.","visualIntent":"Two small sketches of the curve side by side. Left, 'rate 0.1': short arrow from 3 to 2.4. Right, 'rate 1': arrow jumping from 3 to −3 and back, labelled 'bounces forever'.","narrationSummary":"Step size matters. With rate zero point one, x only moves from three to two point four. With rate one, it jumps to minus three and bounces forever.","facts":[{"text":"rate 0.1: 3 − 0.1 × 6","value":2.4,"provenance":"computed"},{"text":"rate 1: 3 − 1 × 6","value":-3,"provenance":"computed"}],"illustration":false}],"substitutions":[],"limitations":["Uses one simple curve with a single lowest point; real problems have many variables and can have several valleys.","The learning rate values are illustrative, chosen so the arithmetic stays clean."]},"scenes":[{"schema":"whiteboard-scene/1","sceneId":"s1","primitives":[{"id":"title","kind":"equation","color":"#222222","width":3,"x":80,"y":90,"size":56,"text":"f(x) = x²"},{"id":"curve","kind":"graph","color":"#1f5fbf","width":5,"x":360,"y":160,"w":1200,"h":780,"domain":[-3.5,3.5],"range":[0,12.25],"points":[[-3.5,12.25],[-3,9],[-2.5,6.25],[-2,4],[-1.5,2.25],[-1,1],[-0.5,0.25],[0,0],[0.5,0.25],[1,1],[1.5,2.25],[2,4],[2.5,6.25],[3,9],[3.5,12.25]]},{"id":"dot","kind":"ellipse","color":"#d62828","width":8,"cx":1474,"cy":367,"rx":14,"ry":14},{"id":"dotLabel1","kind":"text","color":"#d62828","width":3,"x":1595,"y":345,"size":40,"text":"x = 3"},{"id":"dotLabel2","kind":"text","color":"#d62828","width":3,"x":1595,"y":395,"size":40,"text":"height 9"},{"id":"minCircle","kind":"ellipse","color":"#2a9d3f","width":5,"cx":960,"cy":940,"rx":32,"ry":32},{"id":"minLabel","kind":"text","color":"#2a9d3f","width":3,"x":1010,"y":960,"size":40,"text":"minimum"}],"beats":[{"id":"b1","narration":"Gradient descent finds a curve's lowest point.","reveals":["title","curve"],"pauseFrames":10},{"id":"b2","narration":"Stand on this hill at x equals three.","reveals":["dot","dotLabel1","dotLabel2"],"pauseFrames":10},{"id":"b3","narration":"Walk downhill, step by step.","reveals":["minCircle","minLabel"],"pauseFrames":15}]},{"schema":"whiteboard-scene/1","sceneId":"s2","primitives":[{"id":"rule","kind":"text","x":100,"y":300,"size":64,"text":"new x = x − rate × slope","color":"#1a1a1a","width":3},{"id":"slopeq","kind":"text","x":100,"y":480,"size":60,"text":"slope of x² = 2x","color":"#1f4fbf","width":3},{"id":"calc","kind":"text","x":100,"y":620,"size":56,"text":"at x = 3: 2 × 3 = 6","color":"#1f4fbf","width":3},{"id":"curve","kind":"graph","x":1000,"y":300,"w":800,"h":600,"domain":[-3.5,3.5],"range":[0,12.25],"points":[[-3.5,12.25],[-3,9],[-2.5,6.25],[-2,4],[-1.5,2.25],[-1,1],[-0.5,0.25],[0,0],[0.5,0.25],[1,1],[1.5,2.25],[2,4],[2.5,6.25],[3,9],[3.5,12.25]],"color":"#333333","width":3},{"id":"dot","kind":"ellipse","cx":1743,"cy":459,"rx":12,"ry":12,"color":"#d03030","width":6},{"id":"tangent","kind":"line","x1":1686,"y1":606,"x2":1800,"y2":312,"color":"#e07b00","width":5},{"id":"slopelbl","kind":"text","x":1430,"y":380,"size":44,"text":"slope 6","color":"#e07b00","width":2},{"id":"step","kind":"arrow","x1":1720,"y1":505,"x2":1600,"y2":570,"color":"#2a9d4a","width":5},{"id":"ratelbl","kind":"text","x":1300,"y":480,"size":44,"text":"rate = 0.25","color":"#2a9d4a","width":2}],"beats":[{"id":"b1","narration":"The rule: step against the slope.","reveals":["rule"],"pauseFrames":10},{"id":"b2","narration":"For x squared, slope is two x: six at three, pointing uphill.","reveals":["slopeq","calc","curve","dot","tangent","slopelbl"],"pauseFrames":10},{"id":"b3","narration":"So step downhill, scaled by a learning rate of a quarter.","reveals":["step","ratelbl"],"pauseFrames":15}]},{"schema":"whiteboard-scene/1","sceneId":"s3","primitives":[{"id":"curve","kind":"graph","color":"#222222","width":3,"x":100,"y":120,"w":900,"h":840,"domain":[-3.5,3.5],"range":[0,12.25],"points":[[-3.5,12.25],[-3,9],[-2.5,6.25],[-2,4],[-1.5,2.25],[-1,1],[-0.5,0.25],[0,0],[0.5,0.25],[1,1],[1.5,2.25],[2,4],[2.5,6.25],[3,9],[3.5,12.25]]},{"id":"d0","kind":"ellipse","color":"#d62828","width":4,"cx":936,"cy":343,"rx":10,"ry":10},{"id":"h0","kind":"text","color":"#d62828","width":2,"x":960,"y":330,"size":40,"text":"9"},{"id":"a1","kind":"arrow","color":"#1d4ed8","width":4,"x1":930,"y1":355,"x2":750,"y2":795},{"id":"d1","kind":"ellipse","color":"#d62828","width":4,"cx":743,"cy":806,"rx":10,"ry":10},{"id":"h1","kind":"text","color":"#d62828","width":2,"x":770,"y":800,"size":40,"text":"2.25"},{"id":"r1","kind":"text","color":"#1d4ed8","width":2,"x":1120,"y":300,"size":52,"text":"3 − 0.25×6 = 1.5"},{"id":"a2","kind":"arrow","color":"#1d4ed8","width":4,"x1":737,"y1":816,"x2":652,"y2":912},{"id":"d2","kind":"ellipse","color":"#d62828","width":4,"cx":646,"cy":921,"rx":9,"ry":9},{"id":"h2","kind":"text","color":"#d62828","width":2,"x":685,"y":930,"size":36,"text":"0.5625"},{"id":"r2","kind":"text","color":"#1d4ed8","width":2,"x":1120,"y":430,"size":52,"text":"1.5 − 0.25×3 = 0.75"},{"id":"a3","kind":"arrow","color":"#1d4ed8","width":3,"x1":640,"y1":92